{"1-4":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G2992","lemma":"λαός","tr":"laos","gloss":"a people","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"G1278","lemma":"διαπονέω","tr":"diaponeō","gloss":"be vexed","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G2073","lemma":"ἑσπέρα","tr":"hespera","gloss":"evening","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G5084","lemma":"τήρησις","tr":"tērēsis","gloss":"jail","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"G4755","lemma":"στρατηγός","tr":"stratēgos","gloss":"officer","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"G0839","lemma":"αὔριον","tr":"aurion","gloss":"tomorrow","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"G4523","lemma":"Σαδδουκαῖος","tr":"Saddoukaios","gloss":"Sadducee","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"G0706","lemma":"ἀριθμός","tr":"arithmos","gloss":"number","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"G1911","lemma":"ἐπιβάλλω","tr":"epiballō","gloss":"to put on","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"G2605","lemma":"καταγγέλλω","tr":"katangellō","gloss":"to proclaim","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":18}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LUK","chapter":22,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"And Judas went to discuss with the chief priests and temple officers how he might betray Jesus to them.","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":17,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Some Epicurean and Stoic philosophers also began to debate with him. Some of them asked, “What is this babbler trying to say?” Others said, “He seems to be advocating foreign gods.” They said this because Paul was proclaiming the good news of Jesus and the resurrection.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":2,"verse":41,"verseEnd":41,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Those who embraced his message were baptized, and about three thousand were added to the believers that day.","from":4},{"book":"ACT","chapter":6,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"So they stirred up the people, elders, and scribes and confronted Stephen. They seized him and brought him before the Sanhedrin,","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":23,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Then Paul, knowing that some of them were Sadducees and the others Pharisees, called out in the Sanhedrin, “Brothers, I am a Pharisee, the son of a Pharisee. It is because of my hope in the resurrection of the dead that I am on trial.”","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":23,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"A great clamor arose, and some scribes from the party of the Pharisees got up and contended sharply, “We find nothing wrong with this man. What if a spirit or an angel has spoken to him?”","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"When the captain of the temple guard and the chief priests heard this account, they were perplexed as to what was happening.","from":1},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"At that point, the captain went with the officers and brought the apostles—but not by force, for fear the people would stone them.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"5-12":{"people":[{"id":"alexander-g0223h","name":"Alexander","kind":"person","brief":"From Levi","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"annas-g0452","name":"Annas","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"caiaphas-g2533g","name":"Caiaphas","kind":"person","brief":"A High Priest","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"john-g2491i","name":"John","kind":"person","brief":"From Levi","count":1,"firstVerse":6},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":5},{"id":"nazareth-g3478","name":"Nazareth","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":10}],"words":[{"base":"G3686","lemma":"ὄνομα","tr":"onoma","gloss":"name","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":229},{"base":"G4169","lemma":"ποῖος","tr":"poios","gloss":"what?","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":33},{"base":"G0758","lemma":"ἄρχων","tr":"archōn","gloss":"ruler","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":37},{"base":"G4245","lemma":"πρεσβύτερος","tr":"presbuteros","gloss":"elder: Elder","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":65},{"base":"G4982","lemma":"σῴζω","tr":"sōzō","gloss":"to save","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":105},{"base":"G2992","lemma":"λαός","tr":"laos","gloss":"a people","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"G5259","lemma":"ὑπό","tr":"hupo","gloss":"by","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":219},{"base":"G2108","lemma":"εὐεργεσία","tr":"euergesia","gloss":"good deed","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"G0452","lemma":"Ἄννας","tr":"Annas","gloss":"Annas","lang":"g","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"G0444","lemma":"ἄνθρωπος","tr":"anthrōpos","gloss":"a human","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":550}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":14,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":155,"source":"both","text":"Jesus answered, “I am the way and the truth and the life. No one comes to the Father except through Me.","from":12},{"book":"1CO","chapter":3,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":105,"source":"both","text":"For no one can lay a foundation other than the one already laid, which is Jesus Christ.","from":12},{"book":"JHN","chapter":3,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":102,"source":"both","text":"Whoever believes in the Son has eternal life. Whoever rejects the Son will not see life. Instead, the wrath of God remains on him.”","from":12},{"book":"1TI","chapter":2,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":93,"source":"openbible","text":"For there is one God, and there is one mediator between God and men, the man Christ Jesus,","from":12},{"book":"1TI","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":93,"source":"openbible","text":"who gave Himself as a ransom for all—the testimony that was given at just the right time.","from":12},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":89,"source":"openbible","text":"And this is that testimony: God has given us eternal life, and this life is in His Son.","from":12},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":89,"source":"openbible","text":"Whoever has the Son has life; whoever does not have the Son of God does not have life.","from":12},{"book":"LUK","chapter":24,"verse":47,"verseEnd":47,"votes":55,"source":"openbible","text":"and in His name repentance and forgiveness of sins will be proclaimed to all nations, beginning in Jerusalem.","from":12}],"notes":[{"id":"ps-118-22","title":"The stone the builders rejected","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":6},{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"john-baptist-circle","title":"John the Baptist's Circle","people":2},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2}]},"13-22":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"john-g2491h","name":"John","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"peter-g4074g","name":"Peter","kind":"person","brief":"An apostle","count":2,"firstVerse":13}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem-h3389","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":16}],"words":[{"base":"G0444","lemma":"ἄνθρωπος","tr":"anthrōpos","gloss":"a human","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":550},{"base":"G1909","lemma":"ἐπί","tr":"epi","gloss":"upon","lang":"g","inPassage":5,"uses":885},{"base":"G4119","lemma":"πλείων, πλεῖον","tr":"pleiōn, pleion","gloss":"greater","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":45},{"base":"G1096","lemma":"γίνομαι","tr":"ginomai","gloss":"to be","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":668},{"base":"G4592","lemma":"σημεῖον","tr":"sēmeion","gloss":"sign","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":75},{"base":"G3367","lemma":"μηδείς","tr":"mēdeis","gloss":"nothing","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":90},{"base":"G4862","lemma":"σύν","tr":"sun","gloss":"with","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":128},{"base":"G2491","lemma":"Ἰωάννης","tr":"Iōannēs","gloss":"John","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":135},{"base":"G1063","lemma":"γάρ","tr":"gar","gloss":"for","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":1041},{"base":"G2992","lemma":"λαός","tr":"laos","gloss":"a people","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":30,"source":"both","text":"But God chose the foolish things of the world to shame the wise; God chose the weak things of the world to shame the strong.","from":13},{"book":"JHN","chapter":7,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"The Jews were amazed and asked, “How did this man attain such learning without having studied?”","from":13},{"book":"MAT","chapter":11,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"At that time Jesus declared, “I praise You, Father, Lord of heaven and earth, because You have hidden these things from the wise and learned, and revealed them to little children.","from":13},{"book":"ACT","chapter":22,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"You will be His witness to everyone of what you have seen and heard.","from":20},{"book":"JER","chapter":20,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"If I say, “I will not mention Him or speak any more in His name,” His message becomes a fire burning in my heart, shut up in my bones, and I become weary of holding it in, and I cannot prevail.","from":20},{"book":"ACT","chapter":5,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":14,"source":"both","text":"But Peter and the other apostles replied, “We must obey God rather than men.","from":19},{"book":"EXO","chapter":1,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The midwives, however, feared God and did not do as the king of Egypt had instructed; they let the boys live.","from":19},{"book":"1CO","chapter":9,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"Yet when I preach the gospel, I have no reason to boast, because I am obligated to preach. Woe to me if I do not preach the gospel!","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"john-baptist-circle","title":"John the Baptist's Circle","people":3},{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":3},{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2},{"id":"bethany-and-friends","title":"Bethany and the Women Around Jesus","people":2},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":2},{"id":"the-twelve","title":"The Twelve Apostles","people":2}]},"23-31":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":2,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"herod-g2264h","name":"Herod","kind":"person","brief":"A Tetrarch","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"pilate-g4091","name":"Pilate","kind":"person","brief":"A Roman ruler","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"G3816","lemma":"παῖς","tr":"pais","gloss":"child","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":24},{"base":"G0040","lemma":"ἅγιος","tr":"hagios","gloss":"holy","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":222},{"base":"G4863","lemma":"συνάγω","tr":"sunagō","gloss":"to assemble","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":59},{"base":"G1909","lemma":"ἐπί","tr":"epi","gloss":"upon","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":885},{"base":"G3954","lemma":"παρρησία","tr":"parrēsia","gloss":"boldness","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":31},{"base":"G4314","lemma":"πρός","tr":"pros","gloss":"to","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":700},{"base":"G3745","lemma":"ὅσος","tr":"hosos","gloss":"just as","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":110},{"base":"G2036","lemma":"εἶπον","tr":"eipon","gloss":"to say","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":926},{"base":"G2992","lemma":"λαός","tr":"laos","gloss":"a people","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"G1484","lemma":"ἔθνος","tr":"ethnos","gloss":"Gentiles","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":162}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":20,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":28,"source":"openbible","text":"For in six days the LORD made the heavens and the earth and the sea and all that is in them, but on the seventh day He rested. Therefore the LORD blessed the Sabbath day and set it apart as holy.","from":24},{"book":"JER","chapter":32,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"“Oh, Lord GOD! You have made the heavens and the earth by Your great power and outstretched arm. Nothing is too difficult for You!","from":24},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":23,"source":"openbible","text":"The kings of the earth take their stand and the rulers gather together, against the LORD and against His Anointed One:","from":26},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":20,"source":"openbible","text":"Why do the nations rage and the peoples plot in vain?","from":25},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":20,"source":"openbible","text":"“I have installed My King on Zion, upon My holy mountain.”","from":25},{"book":"NEH","chapter":9,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"You alone are the LORD. You created the heavens, the highest heavens with all their host, the earth and all that is on it, the seas and all that is in them. You give life to all things, and the host of heaven worships You.","from":24},{"book":"MAT","chapter":21,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":15,"source":"both","text":"If you believe, you will receive whatever you ask for in prayer.”","from":31},{"book":"2CO","chapter":6,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":14,"source":"openbible","text":"Do not be unequally yoked with unbelievers. For what partnership can righteousness have with wickedness? Or what fellowship does light have with darkness?","from":23}],"notes":[{"id":"acts-4-25-ps2","title":"Why do the nations rage?","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":3},{"id":"roman-officials","title":"Roman Officials","people":3},{"id":"royal-line","title":"The royal line: Judah to David to Jesus","people":2},{"id":"high-priestly-family","title":"The High-Priestly Family","people":2}]},"32-37":{"people":[{"id":"jesus-g2424g","name":"Jesus","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":33},{"id":"barnabas-g0921g","name":"Barnabas","kind":"person","brief":"Brother of Mary","count":1,"firstVerse":36},{"id":"levi-h3878","name":"Levi","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":36}],"places":[{"id":"cyprus-h3794h","name":"Cyprus","kind":"place","brief":"In Cyprus","count":1,"firstVerse":36}],"words":[{"base":"G0652","lemma":"ἀπόστολος","tr":"apostolos","gloss":"apostle","lang":"g","inPassage":4,"uses":80},{"base":"G5225","lemma":"ὑπάρχω","tr":"huparchō","gloss":"be already","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":60},{"base":"G4453","lemma":"πωλέω","tr":"pōleō","gloss":"to sell","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":22},{"base":"G5100","lemma":"τις","tr":"tis","gloss":"one","lang":"g","inPassage":3,"uses":530},{"base":"G5342","lemma":"φέρω","tr":"pherō","gloss":"to bear","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":66},{"base":"G4228","lemma":"πούς","tr":"pous","gloss":"foot","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":93},{"base":"G5087","lemma":"τίθημι","tr":"tithēmi","gloss":"to place","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":100},{"base":"G3761","lemma":"οὐδέ","tr":"oude","gloss":"nor","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":141},{"base":"G3173","lemma":"μέγας","tr":"megas","gloss":"great","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":243},{"base":"G1520","lemma":"εἷς","tr":"ehis","gloss":"one","lang":"g","inPassage":2,"uses":343}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"1CO","chapter":1,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":40,"source":"both","text":"I appeal to you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that all of you agree together, so that there may be no divisions among you and that you may be united in mind and conviction.","from":32},{"book":"EPH","chapter":4,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":34,"source":"openbible","text":"with all humility and gentleness, with patience, bearing with one another in love,","from":32},{"book":"EPH","chapter":4,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":34,"source":"openbible","text":"one God and Father of all, who is over all and through all and in all.","from":32},{"book":"1PE","chapter":3,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"Finally, all of you, be like-minded and sympathetic, love as brothers, be tenderhearted and humble.","from":32},{"book":"JHN","chapter":17,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"that all of them may be one, as You, Father, are in Me, and I am in You. May they also be in Us, so that the world may believe that You sent Me.","from":32},{"book":"JHN","chapter":17,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"I in them and You in Me—that they may be perfectly united, so that the world may know that You sent Me and have loved them just as You have loved Me.","from":32},{"book":"PHP","chapter":2,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"Therefore if you have any encouragement in Christ, if any comfort from His love, if any fellowship with the Spirit, if any affection and compassion,","from":32},{"book":"PHP","chapter":2,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":16,"source":"openbible","text":"then make my joy complete by being like-minded, having the same love, being united in spirit and purpose.","from":32}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"jerusalem-church","title":"The Jerusalem Church","people":3},{"id":"paul-circle","title":"Paul's Circle","people":2},{"id":"herod-family","title":"The Herods","people":2}]}}